{
  "$comment": "WelsonJS app assets integrity index. Maps the integrity digest of each WelsonJS application asset to the URL it can be downloaded from, so that an asset identified by its digest can be restored and verified.",
  "name": "WelsonJS app assets integrity index",
  "version": 1,
  "description": [
    "WelsonJS runs the scripts under app/assets with the privileges of the Windows Script Host, so their content must be exactly the content published by the WelsonJS project.",
    "Every asset file under app/assets/js has a sidecar file named \"<file name>.integrity\" next to it (for example, app/assets/js/json2.js.integrity). The sidecar contains a single Subresource Integrity digest that identifies the exact content of the asset.",
    "This index maps each digest in \"hashes\" to the URL that serves that exact content. To restore an asset, read the digest from its sidecar, look the digest up here, download the URL, and use the file only if its digest matches.",
    "Because entries are keyed by content rather than by path, a digest always leads to the same content wherever the file is located or however it is named.",
    "If a digest does not match, do not execute the file. Restore it from the WelsonJS repository or installer, or download it again and verify it again. If the mismatch persists, report it at the support link.",
    "All URLs point to the WelsonJS snapshot server (\"server\"), which serves the files of the WelsonJS repository at the commit in \"source\". The snapshot path includes the full commit hash, so the content behind each URL does not change.",
    "The index and the sidecar files protect assets only as long as they are authentic. Obtain them from the WelsonJS repository or an official WelsonJS installer, and regenerate them whenever the assets change."
  ],
  "project": {
    "name": "WelsonJS",
    "repository": "https://github.com/gnh1201/welsonjs",
    "support": "https://github.com/gnh1201/welsonjs/issues",
    "license": "(GPL-3.0 or MS-RL)"
  },
